sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: A session turn uses separate command and event channels
  accDescr: The client subscribes to a resumable stream, posts a message, and receives a 202 receipt. A dispatcher queues or starts the turn. Runtime events reach every subscriber independently of the POST response.
  participant C as DorkOS app
  participant H as Routes
  participant D as Dispatcher
  participant R as Agent runtime
  C->>H: Open the session stream
  H->>R: Snapshot and subscribe
  R-->>H: Snapshot, live events
  H-->>C: Snapshot, then live events
  C->>H: Post a message
  H->>D: Dispatch
  D->>D: Persist the queue when needed
  D-->>H: Acceptance receipt
  H-->>C: 202 with the canonical session id
  Note over C,D: 202 means accepted. turn_start means running.<br/>The receipt and live events can race.
  D->>R: Start when the session can take a turn
  R-->>H: turn_start, deltas and tools, turn_end
  H-->>C: Ordered events
  Note over H,C: Events fan out to every subscribed client
  C->>H: Reconnect with the opaque resume cursor
  H-->>C: Replay the gap, or a fresh snapshot if the cursor is stale
  Note over C,H: The app resumes over WebSocket. HTTP consumers use SSE.
